When you wield a polearm it consumes both hands
of the wielding slots and also the quiver.  It teaches the
player that it is a distance weapon doing that.  And then
the "f" starts to make sense.

Wield a halberd.  Fire it at an advancing monster.  Get
told that you swung at empty air.  Wonder what's
going on.  Monster comes in range.  Fire at monster.
Whack it.  Monster keeps coming.  Fire at monster.
Get the message about whacking it with the handle.

The "f" works great at a door.



